      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 multi-reference\n\nSeveral images into one FLUX 3 Image call, each named by its position: image 1 is the scene, the rest supply what goes into it.\n\n**input_image** is *image 1*, **input_image_2** is *image 2*, and so on. Socket order is the meaning \u2014 swap two Load Image nodes and the prompt now describes a different request.\n\nWith `aspect_ratio` at **auto** the output takes image 1's frame. Put a different image first, or set the ratio, for another shape.\n\nUp to **10** references in total. Connect one and the next socket appears. References can also be http(s) URLs in `image_urls`, one per line; they are numbered after the sockets.\n\nSay how the images relate: *the person from image 1 wears the jacket from image 2 in the kitchen from image 3*.\n\n`variation` is not sent to the API \u2014 flux-3-image has no seed. It is **fixed** here so a rerun with nothing changed costs nothing; bump it (or set it to *randomize*) for a fresh take. `expanded_prompt` is `result.prompt`, the prompt the model actually used after expanding yours.\n\n## The prompt lives in one node\n\nThe **Shared Prompt** node feeds the prompt in this graph, so there is one\nplace to edit it. It emits a plain string, **not** a list. That is the difference between it and **Prompt\nList**, which would make each node it feeds run once per line and multiply what the graph\ncosts."
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
